0.0.0.31.2 bed-placement experiment log
==========================================
Bed under test (single uniform mechanism, no per-segment logic):
  crates/articul-cli/src/synth.rs level_output(), currently lines 1119-1146
  white xorshift64* noise (fixed seed 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15, deterministic per render)
  through single-pole lowpass, bed_k = exp(-2*pi*6000/sr)
  normalized to -50 dBFS RMS, mixed post-peak-normalize pre-clamp
  (i.e. chain: tamer -> leveler -> 1.10*0.989/maxv peak scale -> bed mix -> clamp)

Two faithful placements of the same bed were measured:

Placement A (as found in tree, exact -50 dBFS final):
  norm -> bed -> clamp
  room_tone full_mean_ratio (bound <= 3.0):
    hello    6.10 -> 1.89   PASS
    annyeong 2.07 -> 5.28   FAIL (new max: g11u11 o 0.00050 -> 0.00700)
    yeobo    7.95 -> 14.37  FAIL (new max: g7u7 o 0.00109 -> 0.00889)
  room_tone RMS (lift bound <= +1 dB): all PASS
    hello    0.183119 -> 0.183130 (+0.0005 dB)
    annyeong 0.103675 -> 0.103742 (+0.0056 dB)
    yeobo    0.114574 -> 0.114635 (+0.0046 dB)
  lateral_zero notch depth (bound >= 6 dB):
    lateral_window_has_notch      got 0.79 dB   FAIL
    hello_interior_window_has_notch got -0.77 dB FAIL
    (other 2 lateral tests pass)

Placement B (bed moved before peak scale: bed -> norm -> clamp):
  room_tone full_mean_ratio:
    hello    6.10 -> 3.24   FAIL (g3u4 0.00012 -> 0.01030, g1u1 -> 0.00318)
    annyeong 2.07 -> 5.03   FAIL (g11u11 o -> 0.00591)
    yeobo    7.95 -> 12.86  FAIL (g7u7 o -> 0.00547)
  room_tone RMS: all PASS (lift <= +0.02 dB; hello 0.181138, annyeong 0.103493, yeobo 0.114771)
  lateral_zero notch depth:
    lateral_window_has_notch        got -0.31 dB FAIL
    hello_interior_window_has_notch got -1.02 dB FAIL

Reading of the numbers:
- The bed floor does not merely lift quiet-segment HF. Its own HF fraction
  imprints ~0.003-0.010 on bed-dominated (quiet) segments, which is ABOVE every
  natural segment value (pre-bed max 0.00152). So on annyeong/yeobo the bed
  CREATES a new max (quiet 'o' nuclei: 0.00050 -> 0.007, 0.00109 -> 0.0089),
  raising max/min instead of compressing it. Placement barely matters
  (5.28 vs 5.03; 14.37 vs 12.86), so this is level/shape physics, not a
  clipping artifact of one placement.
- The -50 dBFS broadband bed fills the 2.5 kHz lateral antiformant: post-bed
  depth ~= bed's own inter-band tilt ~= 0 dB in both placements, vs >= 6 dB
  required. Recovering 6 dB needs the bed ~15 dB quieter (~-65 dBFS), at which
  level the room_tone floor effect vanishes (hello returns toward 6.10).
- Compressing all demos to ratio <= 3.0 with this bed brightness would require
  the bed to dominate even loud segments (bed RMS within ~3 dB of signal),
  violating the +1 dB lift bound and burying the notch entirely.
- Hence the specified bed (LP ~6 kHz at -50 dBFS) cannot satisfy room_tone and
  lateral_zero simultaneously. Design change needed (e.g. darker bed whose own
  HF fraction sits at/below natural minima, or notch-sparing shaping).
  Escalated as NEEDS_CONTEXT; tree restored to found state (placement A).
  No release renders were produced, so no new TIs TIN hash is recorded.
